    "difficulty": "Foundation",
    "difficultyReason": "Each part is direct application: recall the sine or cosine value at a quadrantal angle and take the reciprocal. The only extra demand is recognising that division by zero makes sec 90° and cosec 180° undefined, and that cot 270° is 0. That is slightly more than reading values off a labelled triangle. It is no harder than a calculator evaluation, and clearly easier than finding an angle from an inverse reciprocal ratio.",
